    Typed Swift globals from their storage symbols (`option swifttypes
    on|off`).

    Issue: a Swift global's storage symbol (`$s7callfix3ctrAA7CounterVvp`)
    names its type in its mangling, yet the data object renders under the
    mangled name as untyped bytes: `$s7callfix3ctrAA7CounterVvp._8_8_ = 2`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, the layout arm
    (`kuna_swifttypes::global_variable`): a `Variable` entity's demangled
    type is the typed data object's type.

    P0 assertion: `option swifttypes on|off` (default on; the pass needs
    `swiftmetadata on`).

    Both passes load `swift_call_syms_elf` (symbols kept) with
    `swiftmetadata on`. Pass 1 (`option swifttypes off`): the globals keep
    their mangled names and raw accesses. Pass 2 (the default): `callfix.n`,
    `callfix.acct` and `callfix.ctr` are typed, so the struct global's fields
    print as `callfix.ctr.value` and `callfix.ctr.step`.
-->
